A||||13||ChadMan||Question for T-top Fiero drivers!||||5||
Z||000000||ChadMan||03-11-2001||10:40 AM||||Of those of you with T-tops, how many of them leak?  How hard is it to replace the seals if they do start to leak?<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||northstar87||03-11-2001||12:14 PM||||If i remember right it usually is not the seal that wears out it is the end caps that crack.  Then the tops dont sit on the seal properly.  This is what happened to one of mine.  Check them out.<P><P>------------------<BR>ASE Master Auto Tech and Auto Instructor||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||03-11-2001||04:03 PM||||Mine have never leaked but the drivers side rattles which is annoying.  Haven't figured it out yet, its on my to do list.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jlhuber||03-11-2001||06:25 PM||||I had an '86 GT with the t-tops.  They leaked due to all four of the end caps being broke.  A friend of mine offered to machine a set out of aluminum (sp?) for me at the place he works, but I ended up selling the car before he got started.<P>------------------<BR>--Jess--<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/blackeye2/double0smile.gif">   <BR>If you expect the unexpected, was it really even unexpected in the first place?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GoCartGuy||03-11-2001||11:54 PM||||Speaking of T-Tops, I've been wanting to convert mine.  I've got the stock sunroof in it, but really been dreamin of T's.  A friend of mine suggested that I do a junkyard seearch and find either one with T's in it and cut the roof off to replace mine.  Has anyone done this before.  I'd have my body shop to the replace, but other than that any tips?<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||03-12-2001||08:39 AM||||Thanks, you guys!  The salesman from the lot selling that T-top Formula called me back.  I told him I wasn't interested in the car and he asked me the tried-and-true salesman question "Would you be interested in the car at any price?"  I gave him a fairly low figure and he said he'd get back with me today.  This car isn't perfect but it is one of 547 original T-top Formulas made.<P>We'll see...||||reg||1
Z||000006||T-top Fiero||03-12-2001||07:45 PM||||GoCartGuy, the chances of finding a T-top Fiero in a junkyard are very low. They are out there but it is a "being in the right place at the right time" kind of thing. I, along with other members of our club have come across 3 T-top Fieros in local junkyards. Even if you find one the odds aren't very good that all pieces will be in usable condition.<BR>If you do find one in good shape it is a very doable conversion. I have done 2 installations, one on my car and one on another members car.<P>Good luck in your search.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GoCartGuy||03-12-2001||08:33 PM||||As far as usable and unusable pieces, what are the chances of finding replacement parts?||||reg||1
Z||000008||T-top Fiero||03-12-2001||09:17 PM||||The drivers side main glass/door seal is no longer available as well as the trim caps that the the glass assembly latches to. Fieroparts.com has the remaining stock of T-top parts available.||||reg||1
Z||000009||pollock||03-13-2001||01:00 AM||||They'll probably leak.....<BR>But it's really hard to replace something if you can't buy a new one!<P>Hey T-top fiero--<BR>I figured I was the only guy in DFW that had done one of these installs on a fiero.  I'm in Denton.<P>I just checked Fieroparts.com, and they still list the corner trim.  Have you called them and found out otherwise?  <P>All 4 of mine are badly cracked.  I was thinking of fixing them and beefing them up with fiberglass, molding them into the A- and B-pillar trim, and covering the assemblies with tweed.  Any thoughts?  <P>Also, I could have sworn I saw a post on here many months ago where Tom, who i guess does plastic work professionally, was talking about reproducing these pieces.  I searched and couldn't find it though.<P>I'll email you later...||||reg||10
Z||000010||RossT||03-13-2001||01:12 AM||||yes TOM did say he might try to make the end caps but that was well over a year ago.  He has been busy and has not posted in a long time.<P>I think that fieroparts.com sold the last set of endcaps on e-bay about a month ago.  I bought one of the last sets they had (just in case). You might want to take yours into a plastic repair guy, and have them repaired.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroparts.com||03-13-2001||07:14 AM||||We did sell the last set, but we still have:<BR>3 left frt. caps <BR>2 left rear caps<BR>2 right rear caps<BR>1 right 88 org. tan frt. cap not sold in a set sold sep. only!<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000012||RobertVol||03-13-2001||01:12 PM||||Can I assume we are referring to the end caps that crack at the screw in point on the plastic trim were they lock in on the rear? If so I need 1 for both sides. How much ? and what color? Well color is really not an issue I have the dye match for the beachwood interior so no problem. <P>BTW.. P seals in yet? Price? I am ready to place that order!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||T-top Fiero||03-13-2001||07:28 PM||||I was fortunate enough to have bought my trim caps and other assorted T-top parts from Farmont Skylite before they sold the stock that they had to fieroparts.com. This was about two years ago. Prices for the trim pieces were very reasonable then. As an example the trim caps were $8 apiece. I am glad I got everything I needed back then.||||reg||1
